							<p align="center"><font size="5"><strong><img src="/pics/1602/Misc/RatheGames.jpg" /></strong></font></p> <p align="center"><font size="5"><strong>The Games</strong></font></p> <p align="center"><font size="5"><font size="3">A Scavenger hunt, a duel and a race are all part of The Rathe Games.&nbsp; All of Norrath is welcome to attend.&nbsp; Invite your friends, your foes, potential members, anyone to come meet us!&nbsp; The Rathe Games are meant for enjoyment, they are meant to build our friendships, to provide the competition every family needs within itself and with others in its community.</font></font></p> <p align="center"><strong><font size="5">The Origin of the Rathe Games</font></strong></p> <p align="center">The Rathe Games began within Binded Souls.&nbsp; They were dreamed up by a couple of elves who wanted to get to know their family better.&nbsp; The original Games were held in Sanctus Seru.&nbsp; Not once, but twice this city housed our Games.&nbsp; It is a lovely city, with many things readily available.&nbsp; It came to our attention that many of our more evil counterparts were not able to attend the Games because the people of Sanctus Seru so hated them.&nbsp; As we love all of our family, evil and good alike, the Seru Games became the Rathe Games.</p> <p align="center"><font size="5"><strong><img src="/pics/1602/lines_blue.gif" /></strong></font></p> <p align="center"><font size="5"><strong>&nbsp;Scavenger hunt</strong></font></p><strong></strong> <p align="center"><br />The scavenger hunt consists of about 10 items you'll need to find throughout Norrath.&nbsp; They're not located in any zone you need a certain level or flag to enter.&nbsp; As there are many items to find you may have a partner.&nbsp; You're not permitted to enter the Bazaar, but you're allowed anywhere else in Norrath.&nbsp; All levels are welcome for the scavenger hunt, and you may choose your own partner.&nbsp; I ask that you remove your roleplay and anonymous statuses to allow me to follow your progress through the games.&nbsp; </p> <p align="center"><br /><strong><font size="5">The Duel</font></strong></p><strong></strong> <p align="center"><br />This will be an open duel.&nbsp; There will be 1&nbsp;winner for each of these categories: </p> <ul> <li> <div align="center">Levels 1-10</div> <li> <div align="center">Levels 11-20</div> <li> <div align="center">Levels 21-30</div> <li> <div align="center">Levels 31-40</div> <li> <div align="center">Levels 41-45</div> <li> <div align="center">Levels 46-50</div> <li> <div align="center">Levels 51-55</div> <li> <div align="center">Levels 56-59</div> <li> <div align="center">Levels 60-65 by individual level. (ie, all levels 60 together, all levels 61 together.)</div> <li> <div align="center">Levels 66-70 is in groups of 3.</div></li></ul> <p align="center">Its up to you what alliances/agreements you make with anyone, just keep in mind that you'll have to&nbsp;eventually kill&nbsp;your parnter if you make one, so be wary.&nbsp; Its the last one standing that wins.</p> <p align="center"><br /><strong><font size="5">The Race</font></strong></p><strong></strong> <p align="center"><br />The race location will be announced just before the race begins.&nbsp; Everyone will get sow, no bard speed, or soe is allowed. </p> <p align="center"><font size="5"><strong>The Auction</strong></font></p> <p align="center">Occasionaly, members are auctioned off.&nbsp; All proceeds go to the guild bank, rather like a fund-raising project.&nbsp; One hour of the member's time is "purchased" for questing, or powerleveling, or other in game related things.&nbsp;</p>
							
